 ## Background
-Implementations such as the one by skanti use OpenGL Geometry Shaders to rasterize triangles directly into a 3D texture [S4, unofficial]. It builds on the concept of using the GPU's rasterization pipeline for volume generation, avoiding the need for CPU-side traversal or complex compute shader logic [S2, S4, unofficial]. The method differs from compute shader-based voxelization by relying on the GPU's rasterization pipeline to determine which voxels are covered, rather than explicitly iterating over a bounding box [S2, unofficial].
